From: Qingping Zhu <qingping_smile@163.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:53:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(contextdb): add workspace, member and API key management
 via extensions

Based on official Hindsight Release v1.0.0
(39c65ffe2f140d0c84cee58566cad8900c5b9908), with one feature commit
for review against the unchanged release baseline.

Resource and permission model:
- Add instance users and multiple API keys with unified PostgreSQL/HMAC
  authentication for administrator and business credentials.
- Grant per-workspace read/read-write access or all current/future spaces;
  keep administrator-only UI login separate from its server-side API key.
- Map readable Bank IDs to independent PostgreSQL schemas. Keep immutable
  workspace identities for grants, asynchronous jobs and delete/recreate.
- Initialize metadata at version 1 with name constraints, foreign keys,
  batched grants, bounded connection budgets and optimistic concurrency.
- Record successful management changes in audit_events. Customer-facing
  audit querying and business-operation audit coverage are not delivered.

Extension and native integration:
- Use Tenant, OperationValidator, HTTP and MCP extension entrypoints with
  shared repository authentication and operation policy.
- Wrap the native app with the extension-owned ASGI admission factory;
  resolve each MCP message credential through FastMCP's public Request.
- Preserve native Recall/Retain/Reflect algorithms and public contracts.
  Protect queue submission, complete Worker execution, final status writes
  and uncertain faults against workspace deletion and name reuse.
- Native Python runtime integration is seven files, +234/-43 lines.
  Preserve raw Bank lifecycle restrictions and privileged diagnostics.
- Keep native Audit/LLM Trace body writes and Webhooks disabled until
  detached writes have complete workspace generation/lifetime protection.

UI and deployment:
- Add workspace/user/key views, masked key lists, one-time issuance,
  fixed-target management proxies and shared ContextDB translations.
- Support a supervised API/in-process Worker plus UI container with external
  PostgreSQL and existing Huawei MaaS-compatible model adapters.
- Require vector, pg_trgm and btree_gin in the RDS examples. Use native
  English full-text; Chinese semantic recall is available while Chinese
  keyword tokenization remains a separate production decision.
- Keep managed settings in the extension template and native env templates
  unchanged. Move official-image deployment helpers and their three tests
  to ContextDB-Research rather than shipping them in this extension.

CI and verification:
- Fix extension import classification consistently across working directories
  and configure CI to use the extension's inherited Ruff settings.
- Explicitly disable environment proxies for node readiness checks.
- Configure pytest's plugin source path for in-process system-test bootstrap,
  independently of the API/Worker subprocess environments.
- Fix standalone OpenAPI generation and test it without deployment secrets.
- Latest completed checks: 438 extension tests passed, one skipped;
  67 ContextDB system tests and 11 native HTTP-session tests passed.
  Root lint, extension Ruff/format and type checks passed.
- Earlier validation also covered 506 targeted native regressions, 414 UI
  tests, production UI build and eight embedded-template checks. These are
  targeted local results, not a completed full upstream or provider matrix.
- PR CI on the previous head exposed absent provider credentials; configure
  and rerun those jobs separately. No claim of an all-green remote pipeline.

Review boundaries:
- Keep shared-authentication query consolidation, test dependency isolation,
  optional deployment scope and Chinese full-text as explicit design TODOs.
- Human design, TODOs, deployment and operations documents live in
  ContextDB-Research; code retains documentation links and machine contracts.

